  "body": "Stacked on #2819.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added `cam.insertText` in `crates/app/src/script/text.rs`. The verb exposes the existing `InsertText` command to the job script runtime.\n- Updated `crates/app/src/mcp/sketch_tools.rs` to dispatch through `text::v_insert_text`, keeping script and MCP behaviors identical.\n- Registered the `insertText` verb in `crates/app/src/script/mod.rs` and defined the `TextProfile` interface.\n- Synchronized `assets/scripts/cam.d.ts` with the updated verb table.\n- Added the `insert_text` tool row to `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Refusals by name\n\n- An empty text or missing arguments.\n- A character with no glyph in the stroke font.\n- A missing `height` parameter, or cap height outside 0.5 mm to 1000 mm.\n- A placement that is not finite or outside 1e6 mm.\n- Unknown options passed in the options object.\n- A setup that does not exist or has no stock.\n- A profile name that is reserved or already in use.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pinned by `crates/app/tests/insert_text.rs`:\n  - `script_verb_places_text_and_undoes_and_checks_inputs`: verifies `cam.insertText` placement, properties, chain counts, undo behavior, and named refusals.\n  - `typed_text_lands_as_a_placed_profile_and_undoes`\n  - `bad_text_and_bad_places_are_refused_by_name_and_nothing_lands`\n  - `a_text_profile_saves_and_loads_with_its_strokes_and_place`\n  - `the_mcp_tool_places_text_reports_it_and_takes_an_engrave_operation`\n- Pinned by `crates/app/tests/scripting.rs`:\n  - `the_bindings_file_is_the_verb_table`: verifies that `assets/scripts/cam.d.ts` matches `script::bindings()`.\n- Clippy: passed cleanly with `-D warnings` on all targets in `camcraft-app`.\n- Code review: run through CodeRabbit CLI (`coderabbit review --agent`), completed with 0 findings.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Toolpath generation and G-code posting from profile chains (refused on main until #1869).\n- Graphical UI dialog for text entry.\n\nChangelog: The cam.insertText script verb places typed text as engraving strokes, and the insert_text MCP tool is documented.\n\nRefs #2679\nFixes #2891\n",
